+covariance do not imply Gaussian diffuse local-filling limits: the current
+construction is the witness. Individual lifted derivative bounds do not
+automatically bound the derivatives of their normalized winding mixture:
+exact mixture terms and a free circle show the missing contribution. A
+static Ward-sector Gaussian limit alone does not establish a photon pole:
+independent gapped rotors supply a comparator.
+
+No statement here rules out the actual compact Hamiltonian's phase, all
+normalization strategies, the framework axioms, or a different source map.
+Formal negative-claim packet PASS is not claimed; see the linked checklist
+in each source note.
