+# Compact source weights and a restricted actual-law Gaussian limit
+
+Author proposals, personally executed without subagents. Surface status:
+`conditional-support`; scientific acceptance and integration are pending.
+The source base is6dda46fc1af02827e9c6b64b2f7d05c381a3ce07. The packet is
+self-contained for its claims; previous campaign PRs motivate the question
+but their unreviewed phase or derivative estimates are not proof inputs.
+
+The preceding comparison law had a Gaussian magnetic limit, while the actual
+compact law retained winding and normalized-weight obligations. This packet
+separates those obligations and obtains a restricted result using the actual
+cosine weight. It does not claim a complete compact photon phase.
+
+## Review units
+
+1. [Actual compact sine scores](notes/COMPACT_SINE_SCORE_DOMINATION_AND_STATIC_CURL_LIMIT.md).
+   Positive electric-walk weights prove a volume-independent exponential
+   bound for time-dependent sine observables at finite temperature. Exact
+   static curl shifts give a quantitative Gaussian limit when a weighted
+   cosine contact average concentrates. A supplied stationary ergodic
+   thermal Gibbs path state supplies that concentration for smooth diffuse
+   curl tests. Principal flux, general time dependence, ground-state passage
+   and a photon pole are not thereby obtained.
+2. [Exact cover and source identities](notes/EXACT_COMPACT_COVER_AND_SOURCE_IDENTITIES.md).
+   Every interval winding, the initial fundamental cell, Haar normalization
+   and the final temporal winding remain in the exact trace. Background
+   derivatives retain their contact and mixture terms. A free circle checks
+   the failure of inheriting convexity or cubic bounds by dropping winding
+   fluctuations. These are standard finite-graph tools, without a novelty
+   claim for covering kernels or Ward identities.
+3. [Sparse-loop counterexample](notes/SPARSE_LOOPS_WITH_NONGAUSSIAN_FILLING_FLUCTUATIONS.md).
+   An explicitly constructed stationary ergodic symmetric current has
+   arbitrarily rare isolated unit loops and diagonal bounded covariance.
+   Its diffuse local-filling observable nevertheless converges to a product
+   of four Gaussians plus independent Gaussian noise, with fourth cumulant
+   78rho^4 and exploding real MGFs. This refutes a specific inference from
+   sparse geometry, not the Hamiltonian law or the framework axioms.
+
+## Verification and interpretation
+
+The [personal review](review/PERSONAL_REVIEW.md) describes the proof checks,
+coverage and limits. Three primary programs compare independent finite
+constructions; their exact source and paired output hashes are recorded in
+the [focused report](review/FOCUSED_VERIFY.json). Nine deliberately changed
+formulas are rejected at disclosed assertions. The first torus Fourier
+refinement failure is preserved and the cutoff is increased without changing
+the criterion. A separately discovered enlarged-box adjacency error was
+corrected by increasing block separation; the earlier passing check and
+source remain preserved. These are author checks, not independent scientific review.
+
+Run the three programs under evidence/ from repository root. The respective
+`AUDIT_TIMEOUT_SEC` contracts are120 seconds. NumPy, SciPy and mpmath are used;
+the sparse-loop enumerator uses only the standard library. Raw outputs are
+not canonical audit cache envelopes. See [reproduction](review/PERSONAL_REVIEW.md),
+[conformance](REVIEW_HISTORY.md), [premises](ASSUMPTIONS_AND_IMPORTS.md),
+[negative-claim discipline](NO_GO_DISCIPLINE_CHECKLIST.md),
+[claim scope](CLAIM_STATUS_CERTIFICATE.md), [trace](TRACE_GATE.md) and
+[handoff](HANDOFF.md).
+
+The owner's current direction is to mark completed, reviewed and source-verified
+milestones ready for independent review. Readiness does not grant retained
+status or a landing verdict. No main merge, axiom, primitive, prompt-file or
+governance change is part of this packet.
